Build a new installation, as of 2026 April 21 on Delta
KEY:
unindented sentences are human commands
  intended statements are explicit shell commands


(if you don't already have one, create a parent directory for your xalt work)
example: ncsa_xalt_test_versions/00/

get clone the repo: 
  git clone https://github.com/ncsa/xalt

make a target (install) directory: 
  mkdir target # or some such

set and export shell variable XALT_BASE_DIRECTORY to the target 
  cd target
  export XALT_BASE_DIRECTORY=`pwd`
  echo $XALT_BASE_DIRECTORY

  cd into the repo: cd ../xalt

# Modify Config/Delta_Config.py in the repo to your wishes as far as target executable and paths and hostnames
  cd Config/
  cp Delta_Config.py_headnodetesting  Delta_Config.py


run build script
  cd ../ncsa_build
  module load util-linux-uuid
  export CPATH=${CPATH}:${UTIL_LINUX_UUID_HOME}/include
  ./build_xalt.sh 
that populates the inital target directory

now modify build target for any testing configuration
  cd ../../target/xalt2/xalt_src/Config

If you want to harvest from head nodes, for instance, modify line 17 of file Delta_Config.py in this directory from SKIP TO KEEP
then build again:
  cd ../../../../xalt/ncsa_build/
  export XALT_LOCAL_ONLY="yes"
  ./build_xalt.sh 

create log repository directory
  cd /ncsa_xalt_test_versions/00/
  mkdir -p log_repo/delta

Modify the following in module file in target according to above
(file will be something like: ncsa_xalt_test_versions/00/target/xalt2/module/xalt/3.0.2.lua
########## file module example lines
local base  = "ncsa_xalt_test_versions/00/target/xalt2/xalt/xalt"

-- LOC local record_dir  = "/sw/workload/delta/json"
local record_dir_base = "ncsa_xalt_test_versions/00/log_repo/delta"
local record_dir  = pathJoin(record_dir_base,"json")

-- LOC local apptainer_bind_dir = "/sw/workload/xalt2/xalt/xalt, /sw/workload/delta"
local apptainer_bind_dir = base..", "..record_dir_base
########## end file example lines

add module directory to MODULEPATH
  cd ncsa_xalt_test_versions/00/target/xalt2/module
  export MODULEPATH=$MODULEPATH:`pwd`

check if module is available
  module avail xalt # we should be able to see xalt/3.0.2

ensure uuid is loaded 
  module load util-linux-uuid

load module
  module load xalt
  echo $LD_PRELOAD # to check if xalt is loaded

